/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A tendon of area Ap stressed to fp applies a force P = Ap fp.
   - Δfp is the tendon stress lost in N/mm²; m = Es/Ec is the modular ratio; fc is the concrete stress at tendon level in N/mm²; φ is the creep coefficient; εsh is the shrinkage strain; Es is the steel modulus, about 195,000 to 200,000 N/mm².
   - Mild steel Fe 250 can be stretched to perhaps 200 N/mm².
   - Grade M40 means a characteristic cube strength fck of 40 N/mm² at 28 days.
   - Stronger concrete helps in five ways.
   - Prestressing steel comes in three forms.
   - The stress-strain curve has no yield plateau.
   - Relaxation is the slow loss of stress in steel held at constant length; it grows with the initial stress and the temperature.
*/
